    "context": "As an electric vehicle engineer... I can say that shitty 18650 batteries are not the only bottleneck in vehicle production. If your supply chain is completely dependant on out of date battery technolgy, one small part of an EV,  the vehicle will be postponed a great deal. There are many many facets to vehicle production than 1/5 of the powertrain.\n\"I think the key concept here is future value.  The NAV is essentially a book-keeping exercise- you add up all the assets and remove all the liabilities.  For a public company this is spelled out in the balance sheet, and is generally listed at the bottom.  I pulled a recent one from Cisco Systems (because I used to work there and know the numbers  ;-) and you can see it here: roughly $56 billion...\n) the NAV is what you would get if you liquidated the company instantaneously.  A definition I like to use for market cap is \"\"the current assets, plus the perceived present value of all future earnings for the company\"\"... so let's dissect that a little.\n\"But you also can't use a comparison to a cell phone battery; they are not the same chemistry either despite both having \"\"lithium\"\" in the name, and EVs limit themselves to a far narrower range of charge than a cell phone does.  My point was that Toyota, didn't base their longevity claims on nothing; they did a shitload of testing of their battery before putting it out, and the \"\"you'll need a new pack after five years\"\" crowd was ultimately proved wrong.  GM has made similar claims about the longevity of their packs, based on similar shitloads of research and testing, and I see no reason why they won't ultimately enjoy the same vindication.",
    "statements": [
        "The available evidence does not establish that electric vehicle batteries have insufficient lifespans to support a used electric vehicle market.",
        "One document argues against directly comparing electric vehicle batteries with phone batteries.",
        "The document states that electric vehicle batteries and phone batteries have different chemistries.",
        "The document states that electric vehicles operate within a narrower battery charge range than phones.",
        "The document states that Toyota battery testing supported claims about battery longevity.",
        "The document states that predictions about electric vehicles needing replacement battery packs after five years proved wrong.",
        "The document expresses an expectation that General Motors batteries would achieve longevity similar to Toyota batteries.",
        "The expectation about General Motors battery longevity is an opinion rather than a demonstrated result.",
        "The documents provide no current battery health data for specific electric vehicle models.",
        "The documents provide no battery replacement costs.",
        "The documents provide no figures about the used electric vehicle market.",
        "The available information is insufficient to determine whether current electric vehicle batteries make a particular used electric vehicle a sound purchase."
    ]
}
